  "id": "dead-bug",
  "name": "Dead Bug",
  "definition": "A supine alternating contralateral arm-and-leg drill with the lumbar position held. The unsupported limbs increase the external spinal-extension tendency while the trunk remains still. Hip flexion and shoulder extension from a flexed position describe the return against gravity; knee extension and scapular upward rotation describe the outward reach. These produced actions occur at different points of a repetition, not as a simultaneous concentric phase. Lowering the leg and arm is not relabeled as a hip-extension or shoulder-flexion strengthening action. Abs are primary, obliques secondary, and limb contributors are bounded anatomy-and-mechanics inferences. No quantitative bodyweight fraction is assigned. The app does not separately represent transversus abdominis. Heel taps, weighted versions, hollow holds, crunches and simultaneous four-limb reaches remain excluded.",
